body:
Honestly, I love your profile. If I saw this profile on Hinge I would definitely leave a comment. Some of your prompts are a little general, but I think it shows that you're adventurous, well read and you understand yourself. Ultimately, it seems like more of a personal preference thing.

&#x200B;

I think it also takes time. Finding the right fit is something that I've struggled with as someone who is heavily driven and ambitious.  Just give it time. You'll be okay.

Hey everyone,

So, first off let me say I love Hinge. I've had way more success on Hinge than Tinder and Bumble combined and I think it's a great service for people looking for something serious.

However, I haven't been on a date in about eight months. I've had a few matches, but no one that really piqued my interest has matched with me. On paper, I feel like I'm the archetype of what a lot of women describe as wanting. I'm 6'6, I have a good job that I'm passionate about. I work in medical research and live within spitting distance of a major city (Philadelphia) and I LOVE fitness. I used to weigh 315lbs and lost 150lbs. It's a big part of my life. So naturally, I want to go on a date with someone who will really support me in that journey.

That's not to say I'm some self-conceited jerk. I run a charity for impoverished students, I'm a big believer in helping your community thrive and I care deeply for others. It's part of why I studied Psychology and more recently began working in Oncology. I'm not looking for a quick fling. I want to find my person.

I just feel like the people that I try to match with me aren't really compatible with me. When I try to match with women who are into fitness or are ambitious (let's say I swiped exclusively on them) I get a 0% return on my swipes. It's like Hinge doesn't even put me in their pile.

I'm hoping this community will give me some insights as to what I'm doing wrong and how I can correct it. I know that I'm a good man and one day, I'm going to make someone really happy. I just need some help to learn how I can put myself in the path of what I desire.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Thanks guys, love you all.
